{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-1 and ASM-20: Procurement and receiving are synchronized from a mock connected upstream source for this build; the UI has no file-upload flow and no live upstream connector is assumed.","ASM-21: The source record ID is the identity used for repeated synchronization; the UI presents the returned update and failure outcomes.","Q-4: Lot-level PO costs are presented as allocated in proportion to received head count assigned to each lot.","ASM-2: Calculations use pounds and USD per pound, a US short ton, while the screen retains entered units for display.","Q-5 and ASM-23 are used for wastage projections and estimates, with no separate wastage movement. ASM-3 conflicts by proposing a wastage-based decrement on saved activities; the actual inventory decrement rule remains unresolved and is assigned to API-side behavior rather than asserted by this web spec.","Q-6 and ASM-5: A bunk rate is pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day and planned quantity is that rate multiplied by planned animal count.","Q-7: Feed consumption and FCR use as-fed pounds.","Q-8 and ASM-7: Planned and delivered feed is separately allocated among lots in proportion to their current animal counts in the pen.","ASM-6 and ASM-24: Feeding activities are permitted without a matching plan; linked activities use planned quantity for variance, and a plan mismatch is shown.","ASM-8 and ASM-25: Authorized users can edit or cancel feeding activities and correct weight records; the UI displays accepted API outcomes.","ASM-9 and ASM-22: Lot target weight and measured lot ADG drive projections when available; otherwise the yard expected daily gain is shown as the assumption, with any lot target override applied.","ASM-10 and ASM-26: Feed cost of gain is reported separately; broader ROI uses available allocated purchase costs and sale proceeds and is labeled unavailable when required data is missing.","ASM-11 and ASM-27: Date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters apply to the dedicated feed-to-gain report; lists support filtering and CSV export, with no custom report builder.","ASM-12: Sex is imported when supplied by the source; otherwise it remains unknown and the report filter offers known values only.","ASM-13: Lots and pens with current animal counts above zero are active.","ASM-14: Demo and presentation materials are provided in an in-app view.","ASM-15 through ASM-18: The app targets WCAG 2.1 AA for main flows, the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, online-only operation, and English left-to-right text.","ASM-19: Staging and production environments and a build pipeline are assumed for delivery, but their configuration is not specified as web-screen behavior."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1024 CSS pixels, every page remains usable without horizontal page overflow; touch targets on the 320-pixel viewport are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels.","text":"Every page is responsive across phone, tablet, and desktop widths, and interactive controls are touch-sized on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of sign-in, import, inventory, ration, plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report flows pass the applicable WCAG 2.1 AA automated checks and keyboard-only interaction checks.","text":"Main user flows conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"All specified main flows pass in 8 browser/version combinations: the latest two versions of each of the 4 named browsers.","text":"The web app supports the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"100% of user-facing labels, messages, and navigation in the delivered flows are English and left-to-right.","text":"The web app presents English, left-to-right user-facing text."}],"outOfScope":["API-SIDE: Durable storage and restart persistence for imported records, inventory, rations, plans, activities, measurements, and calculated values; this web spec verifies only the screens and values returned by the API.","API-SIDE: Procurement-source synchronization execution, source-ID deduplication and updates, failed-record processing, PO-line cost allocation, and persistence of PO-to-lot-to-pen relationships; the web requirements verify the synchronization outcomes and mappings displayed to users.","API-SIDE: Inventory movement accounting, wastage application to actual consumption, stock sufficiency enforcement, and atomic rollback of rejected activities; the web requirements verify returned inventory results and errors.","API-SIDE: Calculation correctness for forecasts, ration optimization, inventory projections, feeding costs, lot rollups, weight metrics, FCR, profitability, and recommendations; the web requirements verify the values and recommendations displayed from API responses.","API-SIDE: Enforcing account authentication, role authorization, and server-side permission checks; the web requirements verify sign-in and role-specific screens.","API-SIDE: Supplying or seeding demo records and producing report data; the web requirements verify the supplied sample data and exported report files."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator-managed account exists and the sign-in page is open","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the signed-in user's Administrator or Operator role and the pages available to that role","when":"The user submits that account's email and password"},{"given":"An Administrator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows user, import, and configuration controls to the Administrator, and plan and activity controls to both roles, while showing dashboards and reports to both roles","when":"The user opens user, import, configuration, plan, activity, dashboard, and report pages"},{"given":"An Operator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-1.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows no user-management controls to the Operator","when":"The user opens the user-management page"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide administrator-managed email-and-password accounts, sign-in, and role-specific screens for Administrator and Operator users.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mock source contains PO and receiving records with vendor, cost, head count, weight, breed, age, and source fields","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the imported record fields and the synchronization status for each record","when":"An Administrator starts synchronization"},{"given":"A source record has a source record ID that was imported previously and a source record has failed synchronization","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the updated record outcome for the previously imported ID and the failed record with its error, without presenting the failed record as a successful import","when":"An Administrator starts another synchronization"}],"ears":"When an Administrator requests synchronization, the Feedlot web app shall display imported procurement and receiving records from the mock connected source and the synchronization outcome for each record.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-20","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides one PO line mapped to multiple lots and those lots mapped to pens","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the PO line, each related lot, each related pen, and the pen capacity and current animal count","when":"A user opens the procurement traceability view"},{"given":"The API provides a PO line cost and received head counts assigned to multiple lots","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each lot's allocated purchase cost and assigned head count, with cost allocation proportional to the assigned received head count","when":"A user opens the lot financial baseline"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display traceable relationships from PO lines through lots to pens, including pen capacity, current animal counts, and lot-level purchase-cost allocations.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides a lot target weight, receiving date, and measured ADG","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the target weight, lifecycle milestones, measured ADG, and projected market date","when":"A user opens that lot's lifecycle view"},{"given":"The API provides no usable measured ADG for a lot and provides the yard expected daily gain and any lot-specific target override","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the projected market date, the target weight used, and that the projection uses the yard expected daily gain until measured ADG is available","when":"A user opens that lot's lifecycle view"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display lot lifecycle milestones, target weights, and projected market dates together with the growth assumption used for each projection.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","I-8","ASM-9","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API provides inventory items and their stock movement values","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the item name, category, available quantity, entered unit, cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, opening stock, stock received, stock consumed, and closing stock","when":"A user opens an inventory item"},{"given":"The API provides inventory forecast values and a configured wastage ratio","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows forecast values for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual horizons and shows the configured wastage ratio used in consumption estimates and projections","when":"A user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"An inventory quantity or cost is entered in a unit other than pounds or USD per pound","id":"AC-REQ-5.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the entered unit and the normalized pounds and USD-per-pound values","when":"A user views the item and its calculated inventory values"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide inventory screens for ingredient quantities, units, costs, nutritional properties, storage locations, stock movements, configured wastage, and forecasts across the requested time horizons.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-5","ASM-2","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens the ration editor and ingredient records are available","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved ration's ingredient proportions, dry matter percentage, energy value, intended range, and calculated cost per pound","when":"The user enters a ration name, type, ingredients, proportions, and intended animal type or weight range and saves"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutritional values, intended animal or weight range, and calculated cost per pound.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has entered nutrition or animal-range constraints and available ingredient data is provided","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows candidate ingredient proportions, each candidate's cost, and the trade-offs against the entered constraints","when":"The user requests ration optimization"},{"given":"Candidate mixes are displayed and none has been saved or assigned","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows candidates as unsaved until the user selects a save or assign action","when":"The user views the candidate list"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall present candidate ration mixes generated against user-entered nutrition or animal-range constraints and require a user action to save or assign a candidate.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen has a bunk rate in pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day, a planned animal count, and a selected ration","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the planned quantity as the bunk rate multiplied by the planned animal count, together with the date, pen, ration, feeding time, per-animal quantity, total feed cost, expected energy intake, and plan status","when":"A user generates a plan for a date"},{"given":"A pen contains animals from multiple lots and the API provides the current animal count for each lot","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a separate planned-feed allocation for each lot in proportion to its current animal count in the pen","when":"A user views the generated plan"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall allow users to generate and view dated pen feeding plans from a selected ration, bunk rate, and planned animal count, with feed quantities allocated across the lots in each pen.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-6","Q-8","ASM-5","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen, ration, activity date, and actual delivered quantity are available, with or without a matching plan","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved activity's pen, lot, ration, planned quantity when available, actual quantity, variance calculated as actual minus planned, as-fed feed quantity, feed cost, energy value, inventory result, and feeding status","when":"An Operator saves a feeding activity"},{"given":"A pen contains animals from multiple lots and the API returns lot allocations for an activity","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a separate delivered-feed allocation for each lot and the corresponding lot consumption and cost rollups","when":"An Operator views the saved activity"},{"given":"The API refuses to save a feeding activity, including when available stock is insufficient","id":"AC-REQ-9.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error and does not show the activity as saved","when":"An Operator submits the activity"},{"given":"An activity date has no matching plan for its pen and lot","id":"AC-REQ-9.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the activity as unplanned and displays the plan mismatch","when":"An Operator views the saved activity"}],"ears":"When an Operator records a feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall submit the activity details and display the returned planned-versus-actual variance, inventory result, feed cost, and lot rollups.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-2","ASM-3","ASM-4","ASM-6","ASM-7","ASM-23","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user opens a saved feeding activity","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned corrected or canceled activity and the returned inventory and lot totals","when":"The user edits or cancels the activity and the API accepts the change"},{"given":"The API refuses an edit or cancellation","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error and the existing activity details","when":"An authorized user submits the change"}],"ears":"When an authorized user edits or cancels a saved feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall display the returned activity, inventory, and lot-total outcome.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-2","ASM-8","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Operator opens a lot's weight measurement form","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the saved measurement fields in the lot's dated weight history and trend","when":"The Operator saves a measurement with date, number of animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, gain since the prior measurement, and notes"},{"given":"An authorized user opens a saved weight measurement","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the corrected record and updated weight trend","when":"The user corrects the measurement and the API accepts the change"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall allow Operators to record dated lot weight measurements and display the lot's weight-measurement history and trend.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","Q-2","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies lot metrics for a lot with receiving date, entry and current average weights, feeding events, and target weight","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total feed consumed, FCR using as-fed pounds, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date","when":"A user opens the lot performance view"},{"given":"A new feeding or weight event has been accepted and the API supplies refreshed lot metrics","id":"AC-REQ-12.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the refreshed metric values returned for that lot","when":"A user views the lot performance screen after the event"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display feed-to-gain metrics supplied for each lot, including days on feed, total weight gain, ADG, total feed consumed, FCR, cost of gain, and projected ship date.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-7","ASM-2","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies feed costs, allocated animal purchase costs, and any recorded sale proceeds for a lot","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows feed cost of gain and the available broader lot profitability values, and labels broader ROI unavailable when sale proceeds or other required cost data are missing","when":"A user opens the lot profitability view"},{"given":"The API supplies recommendations based on a lot's feeding and weight trends","id":"AC-REQ-13.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned feeding-adjustment or sale-timing recommendations","when":"A user opens the lot performance view"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall display lot profitability information and feeding or sale-timing recommendations based on the available feeding, purchase-cost, sale, and weight-trend data.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-10","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies operational dashboard data for lots and pens","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows active lots and pens based on current animal counts above zero, animals per lot and pen, feed inventory status, ration usage, and daily bunk rate per pen","when":"A user opens the dashboard"},{"given":"The API supplies planned and actual feeding, weight, energy, and lot-ranking values","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, feed cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and the best- and worst-performing lots","when":"A user opens the dashboard"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide an operational dashboard showing active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, feed-plan execution, feed and weight performance, energy use, and lot rankings.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API supplies feed-to-gain data for multiple lots, including unknown sex where the source did not provide sex","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the resulting lots with ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, and the sex filter offers known values only when unknown sex records are present","when":"A user opens the report and applies date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters"},{"given":"A user has a feed-to-gain report displayed with or without filters","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file is a CSV or PDF, respectively, containing the displayed report data","when":"The user selects CSV export or PDF export"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report that compares lots, applies date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and offers CSV and PDF exports.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-12","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The demo/presentation view is open and sample operational data is available","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows sample data and sections for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding super prompt and other prompts, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis","when":"A user reviews the view"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide a demo and presentation view with sample operational data, the proposed solution and architecture diagrams, demo flow, coding prompts, validation approach, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["Resolve the conflicting ASM-3 and ASM-23 actual-feeding wastage assumptions with the API implementation owner before using inventory decrement results as an acceptance oracle.","Confirm which lot profitability fields and sale inputs are available in the API so the UI can distinguish calculated values from unavailable broader ROI."]},{"assumptions":["Use the mock procurement and receiving source for synchronization; no live integration or upload flow is included (ASM-1, ASM-20).","Use source record IDs to present synchronization outcomes; the UI displays returned update and failure results, while duplicate prevention and imported-record persistence remain API-side behavior (ASM-21).","Normalize calculation weights and feed quantities to pounds and costs to USD per pound, interpret a ton as a US short ton, and retain entered units for display (ASM-2).","Apply wastage ratio to estimates and projections only; do not add a separate wastage movement or include wastage in actual inventory decrements (Q-5, ASM-23). This selects ASM-23 over the conflicting ASM-3 assumption.","Generate planned feed as pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by planned animal count (Q-6, ASM-5).","Allow activities without a matching plan; when a plan is linked, show variance against its planned quantity and show date, pen, or lot mismatch indicators (ASM-6, ASM-24).","Allocate plan and activity quantities across multiple lots in proportion to current animal counts and display a separate allocation per lot (Q-8, ASM-7).","Display edits and cancellations of feeding activities using returned inventory and lot totals; display corrected weight records with returned recalculated metrics (ASM-8, ASM-25).","Use lot target weight and measured ADG for lifecycle forecasts; when usable measured gain is unavailable, use configured yard target weight and expected daily gain and identify the assumptions used (ASM-9, ASM-22).","Show feed cost of gain separately; broader ROI is unavailable until sale proceeds and other relevant costs are supplied, and show recorded sale revenue when available (ASM-10, ASM-26).","Apply date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters to the dedicated feed-to-gain report; filter sex only among known values (ASM-11, ASM-12).","Treat lots and pens with current animal count above zero as active (ASM-13).","Provide mock records and presentation material in an in-app demo/presentation view (ASM-14).","Support WCAG 2.1 AA on main flows and the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox (ASM-15, ASM-16).","The app is online-only, English-only, and left-to-right (ASM-17, ASM-18)."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At 320, 768, and 1280 CSS-pixel viewport widths, all pages have no horizontal overflow; interactive touch targets are at least 44 × 44 CSS pixels at 320 pixels.","text":"Every page shall reflow for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized interactive controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of applicable WCAG 2.1 AA success criteria pass an accessibility audit of the main flows.","text":"The main user flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"100% of the agreed smoke-test scenarios pass on the latest two versions of each of the four named browsers.","text":"The web app shall support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"1 supported interface language: English; 100% of main-flow screens use left-to-right layout.","text":"The interface shall use English text and left-to-right layout."}],"outOfScope":["Live procurement/receiving connectivity and file-upload ingestion; this build uses a mock connected source (ASM-1, ASM-20).","Self-service registration and SSO (Q-3).","Offline feeding and inventory workflows (ASM-17)."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in page is open","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows email and password fields and no self-service registration or SSO controls.","when":"The user inspects the available sign-in controls"}],"ears":"When an administrator-created user opens sign-in, the web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in without self-service registration or SSO options.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator is signed in and user management is open","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows email, password, and Administrator and Operator role values.","when":"The Administrator opens the account form"}],"ears":"When an Administrator opens user management, the web app shall provide controls to create administrator-managed accounts and assign Administrator or Operator roles.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Administrator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows user management, imports, configuration, dashboard, and report controls.","when":"The user opens the main navigation"},{"given":"An Operator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls and does not show user-management, import, or configuration controls.","when":"The user opens the main navigation"}],"ears":"While a user is signed in, the web app shall expose user, import, and configuration controls to Administrators, plan, feeding, and weight controls to Operators, and dashboard and report views to both roles.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The mock source has PO and receiving records available","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The request targets the configured mock source and the screen shows the returned synchronization status and per-record success or failure messages.","when":"An Administrator starts synchronization"},{"given":"The mock source returns a failed record with its source record ID","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows that source record ID and its returned error message.","when":"The synchronization results are displayed"}],"ears":"When an Administrator starts synchronization, the web app shall request procurement and receiving data from the configured mock source and show the returned import outcomes.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-20","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The source response contains a PO line linked to lots and pens","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the PO line, linked lot and pen identifiers, and the available procurement, animal, and pen fields.","when":"A user opens the imported record details"},{"given":"The source response omits an animal's sex","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the sex field as Unknown.","when":"A user opens that animal's imported details"}],"ears":"When imported procurement and receiving records are displayed, the web app shall show their PO-line-to-lot-to-pen traceability, source identifiers, and available vendor, cost, head-count, weight, breed, age, source, capacity, and current-animal-count fields.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-20","ASM-21","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A PO line has a total cost of 1000 USD and two lots assigned 60 and 40 received animals","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows cost allocation values of 600 USD and 400 USD for the respective lots.","when":"A user opens the PO line's lot allocations"}],"ears":"When a PO line is allocated among multiple lots, the web app shall display each lot's purchase-cost allocation in proportion to its received animal head count.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens feed inventory and selects an existing item or the new-item form","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the required inventory fields, retains entered units for display, and shows opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.","when":"The item details are displayed"}],"ears":"When a user opens feed inventory, the web app shall show and allow entry of feed name, category, available quantity, entered unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location, together with opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Inventory, projected consumption, and a wastage ratio are available","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows estimates for all six requested time horizons and the wastage ratio used.","when":"A user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"The displayed stock movement list includes projected consumption and the configured wastage ratio","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows no separate wastage movement.","when":"A user reviews the movements"}],"ears":"When a user requests an inventory projection, the web app shall show daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual estimates with the configured wastage ratio applied to forecast consumption but not as a separate stock movement.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-5","ASM-2","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A ration has multiple ingredients and entered ingredient units and costs","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each ingredient and proportion, ration nutritional values, intended animal range, and cost per pound in USD using normalized calculation units.","when":"A user opens the ration details"}],"ears":"When a user creates or opens a ration, the web app shall show its name, type, ingredient proportions, normalized cost per pound, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and intended animal type or weight range.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has entered optimization constraints","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each returned candidate's ingredient proportions, cost, and trade-offs without marking it saved or assigned.","when":"The user requests candidate mixes"},{"given":"An optimization candidate is displayed","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the candidate as saved or assigned only after the corresponding action is accepted.","when":"The user chooses save or assign"}],"ears":"When a user submits nutrition constraints or animal-range constraints for ration optimization, the web app shall show candidate ingredient mixes with their costs and trade-offs and require an explicit save or assign action before using a candidate.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen plan uses a bunk rate of 25 pounds per animal per day and a planned animal count of 40","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a planned feed quantity of 1000 pounds and the plan's date, pen, ration, feeding time, cost, expected energy, and status.","when":"The user generates the plan"}],"ears":"When a user generates a pen feeding plan, the web app shall calculate planned feed as the bunk rate in pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by the planned animal count and display the plan date, pen, ration, quantity, feeding time, cost, expected energy, and status.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-6","ASM-2","ASM-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen plan is for 1000 pounds and its current animals are split 60 to one lot and 40 to another","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows separate allocations of 600 and 400 pounds for the respective lots.","when":"A user opens the plan's lot allocations"}],"ears":"When a pen plan includes animals from multiple lots, the web app shall show a separate planned-feed allocation for each lot in proportion to that lot's current animal count in the pen.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","Q-8","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Pen plans exist with delivery dates and statuses","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each plan's date, pen, ration, planned quantity, and status.","when":"A user opens feeding schedules"}],"ears":"When a user opens pen feeding schedules, the web app shall show plans by delivery date and pen with their Planned, In progress, Completed, or Skipped status.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An Operator enters a feeding activity for a date and pen with no matching plan","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen allows the unplanned activity to be submitted and shows it as unplanned when accepted.","when":"The Operator submits the activity"},{"given":"An activity does not match the available plan date, pen, or lot","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows a plan-mismatch indicator.","when":"The activity is displayed in a list or detail view"}],"ears":"When an Operator records feeding for a pen, the web app shall allow an activity with or without a matching plan and show a plan-date or pen mismatch when one exists.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-6","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A linked plan is for 900 pounds and an accepted activity records 950 pounds delivered","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows planned feed of 900 pounds, actual feed of 950 pounds, and a variance of 50 pounds, along with the activity fields.","when":"The Operator opens the activity details"}],"ears":"When an Operator records a feeding activity, the web app shall show its date, pen, lot, ration, planned and actual as-fed quantities, actual-minus-planned variance, feed cost, energy value, inventory consumption, and feeding status.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","Q-7","ASM-2","ASM-6","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API response for an accepted activity contains ingredient consumption and multiple lot allocations","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned ingredient quantities, as-fed lot quantities, feed costs, and separate lot allocations.","when":"The activity and affected inventory or lot summaries are displayed"}],"ears":"When the API accepts a feeding activity, the web app shall display the returned ingredient-level inventory consumption and lot-level feed quantity and cost allocations, using the ration mix and current lot head-count proportions.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-6","Q-8","ASM-2","ASM-7","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API refuses an activity for insufficient stock and returns unchanged totals","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error and unchanged inventory and lot total values.","when":"The Operator views the save result"}],"ears":"If the API refuses a feeding activity because available stock is insufficient, then the web app shall show the returned error and the returned unchanged inventory and lot totals.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API accepts an edit or cancellation and returns updated totals","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned activity status and recalculated inventory and lot total values.","when":"The user views the activity and affected summaries"},{"given":"The API refuses an edit or cancellation","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error message.","when":"The user views the action result"}],"ears":"When an authorized user edits or cancels a saved feeding activity, the web app shall display the API's returned corrected or cancelled activity and recalculated inventory and lot totals.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-8","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has a prior dated measurement and a new accepted measurement","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows both dated records and the new measurement's animal count, average and total weights, gain since the prior measurement, and notes.","when":"An Operator opens the lot's weight history"}],"ears":"When an Operator records a lot weight measurement, the web app shall show its lot, measurement date, number of animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, gain since the prior measurement, and notes in a dated weight history.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API accepts a correction to a weight measurement and returns updated values","id":"AC-REQ-20.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the corrected measurement and returned recalculated metrics and trend.","when":"The user opens the lot history and metrics"}],"ears":"When an authorized user corrects a saved weight measurement, the web app shall display the corrected record and the returned recalculated lot metrics and weight trend.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-8","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has measured average daily gain and a lot-specific target weight","id":"AC-REQ-21.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the lot-specific target weight, measured gain basis, and projected market date.","when":"A user opens its lifecycle forecast"},{"given":"A lot has no usable measured gain","id":"AC-REQ-21.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the configured yard target and expected daily-gain assumptions used for its projected market date.","when":"A user opens its lifecycle forecast"}],"ears":"When a user opens a lot lifecycle forecast, the web app shall show target weight and projected market date using lot-specific target weight and measured average daily gain when available, or the configured yard target and expected daily gain until observed gain is available.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-9","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has receiving date, entry and current weights, accepted feeding records, and a positive daily gain","id":"AC-REQ-22.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows days on feed as current date minus receiving date; weight gain as current average weight minus entry average weight; ADG as gain divided by days on feed; total feed as the sum of as-fed feeding quantities; FCR as pounds consumed divided by pounds gained; cost of gain as feed cost divided by pounds gained; and projected ship date from remaining target-weight gain divided by ADG.","when":"A user opens its performance metrics"},{"given":"A feeding or weight event is accepted and the API returns updated lot metrics","id":"AC-REQ-22.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned updated metrics.","when":"The user refreshes or reopens lot performance"}],"ears":"When a user opens lot performance metrics, the web app shall show days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total as-fed feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, cost of gain, and projected ship date using the requested formulas.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-7","ASM-2","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has purchase and feed costs but no sale proceeds or complete relevant costs","id":"AC-REQ-23.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows feed cost of gain and labels broader ROI as unavailable.","when":"A user opens its financial performance"},{"given":"A lot's returned financial data includes recorded sale revenue and relevant costs","id":"AC-REQ-23.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the purchase cost, feed cost, recorded sale revenue, and returned broader profitability values.","when":"A user opens its financial performance"}],"ears":"When a user opens lot financial performance, the web app shall show feed cost of gain separately from broader profitability and show broader ROI as unavailable until sale proceeds and other relevant costs are supplied.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-10","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API returns an operational recommendation and its metric basis","id":"AC-REQ-24.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the recommendation and the returned metric basis.","when":"A user opens lot insights"}],"ears":"When current weight-gain or feeding data supports an operational next step, the web app shall show a feeding-adjustment or sale-timing recommendation with the metric basis displayed.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API returns dashboard data for lots, pens, inventory, rations, plans, activities, and weights","id":"AC-REQ-25.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each requested dashboard metric, and counts a lot or pen as active when its current animal count is above zero.","when":"A user opens the operations dashboard"}],"ears":"When a user opens the operations dashboard, the web app shall show active lots and pens, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily pen bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, total feed and cost, starting and current weights, weight gain, ADG, feed-to-gain, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The API returns metrics for active lots","id":"AC-REQ-26.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.","when":"A user opens the yard-level summary"}],"ears":"When a user opens the yard-level summary, the web app shall show aggregate metrics for active lots including total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The report has lot data including known or unknown sex values","id":"AC-REQ-27.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows ADG, FCR, and cost-of-gain comparison fields and date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, with sex filtering limited to known values.","when":"A user opens the feed-to-gain report"},{"given":"A user selects report filters","id":"AC-REQ-27.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows only rows matching the selected date range, breed, known sex, and pen values.","when":"The report results refresh"}],"ears":"When a user opens the dedicated feed-to-gain report, the web app shall show lot comparisons for ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and provide date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-12"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has applied report filters","id":"AC-REQ-28.1","level":"ui","then":"The browser download list contains a file in the selected format with the filtered report data.","when":"The user chooses CSV or PDF export"}],"ears":"When a user exports the feed-to-gain report, the web app shall provide the filtered report as a CSV or PDF file.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens the demo and presentation view","id":"AC-REQ-29.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows mock operational records and sections for architecture diagrams, demo flow, prompts, validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.","when":"The view finishes loading"}],"ears":"When a user opens the demo and presentation view, the web app shall show mock operational data and materials covering the proposed architecture and diagrams, demo flow, super prompt and other prompts, validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":[]},{"assumptions":["For actual feeding inventory consumption, this draft follows ASM-23 and Q-5: decrement by recorded actual feed quantity, include wastage in estimates and projections only, and do not create a separate wastage movement; this resolves the conflicting ASM-3 assumption.","Lot lifecycle projections use a lot-specific target weight and measured ADG when available; otherwise the configured yard expected daily gain is identified as the assumption used.","Dashboard and report filtering is scoped as stated in ASM-11 and ASM-27; the dedicated Feed-to-Gain report supports date range, breed, sex, and pen filters, with filtered CSV and PDF export.","The application is an online responsive web app, English-only, and uses the mock connected source for procurement and receiving synchronization; it does not provide native mobile apps or file-upload ingestion."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"Viewport checks at 320, 768, and 1440 CSS pixels; primary controls are at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels at 320 CSS pixels.","text":"Every page shall use a responsive layout for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Zero automated WCAG 2.1 AA violations in sign-in, import, planning, feeding, weight entry, dashboard, and report checks.","text":"The main application flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"100% pass rate for the smoke-test suite on the latest two versions of each of the four named browsers.","text":"The web app shall support current browser usage in Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"Exactly 1 supported interface locale, English, rendered left-to-right.","text":"The user interface shall use English text and left-to-right layout."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"Exactly 2 deployment targets, staging and production; each target completes the defined build pipeline successfully.","text":"The web app shall have staging and production deployment targets built through a pipeline."}],"outOfScope":[],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator is signed in and the mock source returns PO and receiving records plus one failed record","id":"AC-REQ-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned PO and receiving fields and the failed record details","when":"The administrator starts synchronization"},{"given":"An administrator is signed in and a source record has changed since the previous synchronization","id":"AC-REQ-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The synchronization request includes the source record ID and the screen displays the returned updated record","when":"The administrator starts synchronization"}],"ears":"When an administrator starts synchronization, the Feedlot web app shall send a synchronization request to the configured mock procurement and receiving source and display returned PO and receiving records with source ID, vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, source, and per-record failures.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-20","ASM-21"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A PO line has a total cost of 10000 USD and returned lot allocations assign 10 and 30 of 40 received animals","id":"AC-REQ-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the PO line linked to both lots and their pens, and displays lot cost shares of 2500 USD and 7500 USD","when":"An administrator opens the entity mapping view"},{"given":"A PO line is linked to a pen with a known capacity and current animal count","id":"AC-REQ-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the pen ID, capacity, and current animal count","when":"An administrator opens that PO line's mapping details"}],"ears":"Where a PO line maps to one or more lots, the Feedlot web app shall display the PO-to-lot-to-pen trace, each pen's ID, capacity, and current animal count, and purchase-cost shares allocated to lots in proportion to their assigned received head counts.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user has an administrator-managed email and password account","id":"AC-REQ-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the signed-in application page","when":"The user submits those credentials on the sign-in page"},{"given":"A visitor opens the sign-in page","id":"AC-REQ-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows email and password fields and does not show self-service registration or SSO controls","when":"The page is displayed"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in for administrator-managed accounts without self-service registration or SSO.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An administrator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows user, import, configuration, plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls","when":"The administrator opens the application navigation and an operational record view"},{"given":"An operator is signed in","id":"AC-REQ-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows plan, feeding, weight, dashboard, and report controls and does not show user, import, or configuration controls","when":"The operator opens the application navigation"}],"ears":"The Feedlot web app shall expose user, import, and configuration controls only to administrators, expose plan, feeding, and weight controls to operators, and expose dashboards and reports to both roles.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has a target weight, receiving date, and measured ADG","id":"AC-REQ-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the target weight, lifecycle milestones, projected market date, and measured ADG as the projection assumption","when":"A user opens the lot lifecycle view"},{"given":"A lot has no usable observed gain and the yard has a configured expected daily gain","id":"AC-REQ-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the projected market date and identifies the configured expected daily gain as the assumption used","when":"A user opens the lot lifecycle view"}],"ears":"When a user opens a lot lifecycle view, the Feedlot web app shall display the lot's target weight, lifecycle milestones, projected market date, and the growth assumption used for the projection.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-9","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory response contains an item with its stock values, entered units, cost, nutrition fields, and storage location","id":"AC-REQ-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the item fields and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"A user opens the feed inventory screen"},{"given":"An inventory item is entered in tons with a cost per ton","id":"AC-REQ-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the entered units and the normalized calculation values in pounds and USD per pound","when":"A user opens its cost details"}],"ears":"When a user opens feed inventory, the Feedlot web app shall display each feed item's category, available quantity, entered unit and cost, dry matter percentage, energy value, storage location, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Inventory, consumption estimates, and a configured wastage ratio are available","id":"AC-REQ-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays projected quantities for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons with wastage included in the estimates","when":"A user opens the inventory forecast"},{"given":"The inventory movement response contains receipts and feed consumption","id":"AC-REQ-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned stock movements and no separate wastage movement","when":"A user opens the movement list and forecast"}],"ears":"When a user requests an inventory forecast, the Feedlot web app shall display projected ingredient quantities for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, six-month, and annual horizons using the configured wastage ratio in consumption estimates and projections without displaying a separate wastage stock movement.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-5","ASM-23"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user enters a ration name, type, ingredient proportions, nutrition values, and animal or weight range","id":"AC-REQ-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned ration with its ingredients, proportions, nutrition values, intended range, and cost per pound","when":"The user saves the ration"},{"given":"A ration's ingredients have costs entered in different supported weight units","id":"AC-REQ-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the calculated ration cost in USD per pound and retains the entered units for display","when":"The user opens the ration cost details"}],"ears":"When an authorized user creates a ration, the Feedlot web app shall accept multiple ingredients with proportions and display the ration's nutrition values, intended animal or weight range, and calculated cost per pound using normalized ingredient quantities and costs.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","ASM-2"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user has entered nutrition or animal-range constraints and the optimizer returns candidate mixes","id":"AC-REQ-9.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each candidate's ingredient proportions, cost, and trade-offs without marking any candidate as saved or assigned","when":"The user requests candidate mixes"},{"given":"Candidate mixes are displayed","id":"AC-REQ-9.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned saved or assigned ration","when":"The user selects and saves or assigns a candidate"}],"ears":"When an authorized user submits nutrition or animal-range constraints for ration optimization, the Feedlot web app shall display candidate ingredient proportions, costs, and trade-offs and require the user to save or assign a selected candidate before it becomes an active ration.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A pen has 100 animals and its bunk rate is 20 pounds as-fed per animal per day","id":"AC-REQ-10.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays a planned feed quantity of 2000 pounds and the selected ration and feeding time","when":"An operator generates a plan for that pen and date"},{"given":"A planned pen contains animals from two lots in a 1-to-3 count ratio","id":"AC-REQ-10.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays separate lot allocations in the same 1-to-3 ratio","when":"An operator generates the plan"},{"given":"The generated plan response includes plan status, total feed cost, and expected energy intake","id":"AC-REQ-10.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the plan date, pen, lot allocations, animal count, ration, planned quantity, feeding time, cost, energy, and status","when":"The operator opens the plan details"}],"ears":"When an operator generates a pen feeding plan, the Feedlot web app shall submit the date, pen, ration, bunk rate, planned animal count, and feeding time and display planned quantity as pounds of as-fed ration per animal per day multiplied by the planned animal count, with separate lot allocations proportional to current lot animal counts in the pen.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-6","Q-8","ASM-5","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A feeding plan for a pen and date specifies 1000 pounds and the operator enters 950 pounds actual delivered","id":"AC-REQ-11.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays planned quantity 1000 pounds, actual quantity 950 pounds, and variance -50 pounds","when":"The operator saves the linked feeding activity"},{"given":"A pen contains animals from multiple lots and the feeding activity response includes lot allocations and inventory consumption","id":"AC-REQ-11.2","level":"ui","then":"The request contains separate lot allocations and the screen displays the returned lot allocations and inventory consumption based on the actual delivered quantity","when":"The operator saves the feeding activity"},{"given":"No matching plan exists for the activity date and the save response is successful","id":"AC-REQ-11.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the activity as unplanned and displays the returned activity and lot totals","when":"The operator saves the feeding activity"}],"ears":"When an operator saves a feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall send the actual as-fed quantity, ration, date, pen, and separate lot allocations, and display the returned planned and actual quantities, actual-minus-planned variance when linked to a plan, feed cost, energy, inventory consumption, and lot consumption and cost totals.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-6","ASM-7","ASM-23","ASM-24"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operator has entered a feeding activity and the feed service returns an insufficient-stock error","id":"AC-REQ-12.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen retains the entered values, displays the returned error, and continues to display the prior inventory and lot totals","when":"The operator saves the activity"}],"ears":"If the feed service refuses a feeding save for insufficient stock, then the Feedlot web app shall retain the entered activity values and display the returned error without displaying updated inventory or lot totals.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized user opens a saved feeding activity","id":"AC-REQ-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned activity state and inventory and lot totals","when":"The user submits an edit or cancellation"}],"ears":"When an authorized user edits or cancels a saved feeding activity, the Feedlot web app shall submit the correction or cancellation and display the returned activity, inventory, and lot totals.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","ASM-8","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operator enters a dated measurement with animal count, average weight, total weight, and notes","id":"AC-REQ-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned measurement in the lot's dated weight trend","when":"The operator saves the measurement"},{"given":"An authorized user opens a saved weight measurement","id":"AC-REQ-14.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned corrected record in the lot's weight trend","when":"The user corrects the original measurement"}],"ears":"When an operator records a lot weight measurement, the Feedlot web app shall submit the lot, measurement date, number of animals weighed, average weight, total lot weight, and notes and display the returned dated measurement in the lot's weight trend.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","ASM-25"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The lot metrics response contains receiving date, entry and current average weights, feeding totals, ADG, FCR, feed cost of gain, target weight, and projected ship date","id":"AC-REQ-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total as-fed feed consumed, FCR, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date","when":"A user opens lot performance"},{"given":"A feeding or weight save returns refreshed lot metrics","id":"AC-REQ-15.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned updated metric values","when":"The user returns to lot performance"}],"ears":"When a user views lot performance, the Feedlot web app shall display returned days on feed, total weight gain, average daily gain, total as-fed feed consumed, feed conversion ratio, feed cost of gain, and projected ship date, and refresh those values after a successful feeding or weight save.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","Q-7","ASM-2","ASM-22"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot has allocated purchase cost and feed cost but no sale proceeds or other relevant costs","id":"AC-REQ-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays purchase and feed cost components, feed cost of gain, and a broader ROI unavailable label","when":"A user opens lot profitability"},{"given":"The recommendation response contains feeding adjustments and a sale-timing recommendation","id":"AC-REQ-16.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned feeding and sale-timing recommendations","when":"A user opens lot insights"}],"ears":"When a user views lot profitability and recommendations, the Feedlot web app shall display feed cost of gain, available purchase and feed cost components, recorded sale revenue when present, an unavailable broader ROI label when sale proceeds or other relevant costs are missing, and returned feeding or sale-timing recommendations.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-8","ASM-10","ASM-26"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard response contains active lot and pen data and the listed operational metrics","id":"AC-REQ-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, feed totals and cost, weight metrics, ADG, FCR, cost per gain, energy, and best- and worst-performing lots","when":"A user opens the operations dashboard"}],"ears":"When a user opens the operations dashboard, the Feedlot web app shall display active lots and pens, animal counts, feed inventory status, ration usage, daily pen bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, weight gain, ADG, FCR, feed cost per gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The report contains multiple lots, including records with unknown sex","id":"AC-REQ-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost of gain and permits filtering known sex values","when":"A user opens the report and selects date range, breed, known sex, and pen filters"},{"given":"A user has applied report filters","id":"AC-REQ-18.2","level":"ui","then":"A downloadable file is produced for the filtered report in the selected format","when":"The user selects CSV export or PDF export"}],"ears":"When a user opens the Feed-to-Gain report, the Feedlot web app shall display ADG, FCR, and cost of gain for multiple lots, allow filtering by date range, breed, sex, and pen, and offer CSV and PDF exports of the filtered report.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-11","ASM-12","ASM-27"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The yard summary response contains aggregate values for active lots","id":"AC-REQ-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost","when":"A user opens the yard summary"}],"ears":"When a user opens the yard summary, the Feedlot web app shall display aggregate total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost across active lots.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Mock demo data and presentation content are available","id":"AC-REQ-20.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays mock operational records and sections for architecture diagrams, demo flow, prompts, validation, challenges, readiness, and go-to-market analysis","when":"A user opens the demo and presentation view"}],"ears":"When a user opens the demo and presentation view, the Feedlot web app shall present mock operational data, the proposed architecture and diagrams, demo flow, super prompt and other prompts, validation approach, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["Confirm the conflict between ASM-3 and ASM-23 with the product owner before implementation; the specification currently follows the later, more specific ASM-23 behavior."]}],"models":["gpt-6-luna","gpt-6-luna","gpt-6-luna"],"notes":[]}